# Everything the import step produces from YOUR disc: the raw image, the files pulled
# off it, and the Japanese script decoded from them. All of it is Sony's copyrighted
# content. This repo is public and ships none of it — a contributor regenerates it
# from their own dump (README § "The import step"). Never commit from here, and never
# copy text out of it into a tracked file beyond a short quoted example.
/disc/
# Third-party reference material kept locally for context (the GameFAQs walkthrough,
# cloned upstream repos). Copyrighted by its authors; README § "Reference material"
# says where to get each piece.
/reference/
# Scratch: dumps, contact sheets, emulator traces, Ghidra projects (a Ghidra database
# embeds the executable, so it is disc content too). What is learned from scratch goes
# in research/; the scratch itself is disposable.
/work/
# Build outputs: patched files, the patched image, and the emitted patch. The patch is
# released through GitHub Releases, not tracked.
/build/
# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
/.venv/
